    {
      "id": "w7v098g",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "SOURCES OF ENERGY"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Sun is the ultimate primary source of energy for almost all forms of energy on Earth, excluding nuclear, tidal, and geothermal energy.",
        "Conventional energy sources like coal and petroleum are exhaustible and contribute heavily to environmental pollution and acid rain.",
        "Solar cells are made of silicon semiconductors and convert sunlight directly into electrical energy via the photovoltaic effect.",
        "Nuclear power plants rely on controlled nuclear chain fission reactions of Uranium-235 or Plutonium-239 to produce thermal energy.",
        "Hydropower converts the potential energy of stored height-bound water into electrical energy without direct greenhouse gas emissions during operation."
      ],
      "id": "a01q0gw"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "Min Wind Speed",
          "value": "15 km/h",
          "icon": "clock"
        },
        {
          "label": "Biogas Methane Content",
          "value": "75%",
          "icon": "check"
        },
        {
          "label": "Solar Cell Voltage Output",
          "value": "0.5-1.0 V",
          "icon": "info"
        },
        {
          "label": "Energy per U-235 Fission",
          "value": "200 MeV",
          "icon": "award"
        }
      ],
      "id": "uylgjxz"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ds7j2b6",
      "content": "Energy is essential for all human activities. "
    },
    {
      "id": "571zjvd",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "1. CHARACTERISTICS OF A GOOD SOURCE OF ENERGY"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ds9ug1w",
      "content": "• High calorific value."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rrabl6s",
      "content": "• Easily available."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3zsxjq7",
      "content": "• Easy to store and transport."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "uzftvgs",
      "content": "• Economical."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ozzqmto",
      "content": "• Causes minimum pollution."
    },
    {
      "id": "q9oahkb",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "2. CONVENTIONAL SOURCES OF ENERGY"
    },
    {
      "id": "6ukk2e9",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Source</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Example</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Fossil Fuels</p>",
            "<p>Coal, Petroleum, Natural Gas</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Thermal Power</p>",
            "<p>Coal-based power plants</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Hydroelectric Power</p>",
            "<p>Dams</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3za3jyp",
      "content": "Fossil fuels are non-renewable and cause pollution."
    },
    {
      "id": "cr3orx3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "3. THERMAL POWER PLANT"
    },
    {
      "id": "hb3duc1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vkz9pfk",
      "content": "• Coal is burnt to produce steam."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tj9hgjy",
      "content": "• Steam rotates turbine."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "21s038p",
      "content": "• Turbine rotates generator to produce electricity."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5d10cm6",
      "content": "• Located near coal fields to reduce transport cost."
    },
    {
      "id": "ljgp20t",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "4. HYDROELECTRIC POWER PLANT"
    },
    {
      "id": "5vrz2tm",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4aw6ck5",
      "content": "• Water stored at height in dam."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "32peg5a",
      "content": "• Potential energy converts into kinetic energy."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "p16pfmw",
      "content": "• Rotates turbine connected to generator."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tzzcj2g",
      "content": "• Renewable and non-polluting."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2398vy9",
      "content": "• Causes ecological imbalance if forests submerged."
    },
    {
      "id": "542d1xq",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "5. NON-CONVENTIONAL SOURCES OF ENERGY"
    },
    {
