          "cells": [
            "<p>Energy Output</p>",
            "<p>Moderate</p>",
            "<p>Very High</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "f7pdiiu",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "11. CALORIFIC VALUE"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nvivt6j",
      "content": "• Calorific value is the amount of heat produced when 1 kg of fuel is completely burnt."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2eqtypw",
      "content": "• Unit: kJ/kg."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yogpdk3",
      "content": "• Higher calorific value → Better fuel."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "p9a4dym",
      "content": "• LPG and CNG have higher calorific value than coal."
    },
    {
      "id": "jbtso5c",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "12. PROBLEMS WITH FOSSIL FUELS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qzg13co",
      "content": "• Non-renewable (limited reserves)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hocr1a9",
      "content": "• Causes air pollution (CO2, SO2, NOx)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gn2503m",
      "content": "• Responsible for global warming."
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Feature",
        "Thermal Power Plant",
        "Nuclear Power Plant"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Fuel Source",
          "Fossil fuels (Coal, Natural Gas, Oil)",
          "Nuclear fuels (Uranium-235, Thorium-232)"
        ],
        [
          "Reaction Mechanism",
          "Chemical combustion of hydrocarbons",
          "Controlled nuclear fission chain reaction"
        ],
        [
          "Energy Density",
          "Low energy released per unit mass of fuel",
          "Extremely high energy released per unit mass"
        ],
        [
          "Waste Generated",
          "Fly ash, carbon dioxide, sulfur oxides",
          "Hazardous radioactive waste requiring deep storage"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "pqlwdis"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "m3fpmog",
      "content": "• Acid rain due to sulphur dioxide."
    },
    {
      "id": "e1h8uli",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "13. THERMAL POWER PLANT – EFFICIENCY CONCEPT"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2pkv9wk",
      "content": "• Large amount of heat energy lost in environment."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mg9vgps",
      "content": "• Efficiency is limited due to heat loss."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8wju3k7",
      "content": "• Coal transportation cost is high, hence plants built near coal mines."
    },
    {
      "id": "mly363m",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "14. HYDROPOWER – EXAM CONCEPTS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "46dwxbz",
      "content": "• Renewable but depends on rainfall."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5rbera6",
      "content": "• Causes displacement of people."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fr673t3",
      "content": "• Siltation reduces efficiency of dams."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qp2per8",
      "content": "• Produces no air pollution."
    },
    {
      "id": "tisyyc9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "15. SOLAR CELL – WORKING PRINCIPLE"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yexpphb",
      "content": "• Based on photovoltaic effect."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4uqvmz5",
      "content": "• Silicon is commonly used semiconductor."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "go5u76r",
      "content": "• Produces DC electricity."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hva7xu9",
      "content": "• Low efficiency but eco-friendly."
    },
    {
      "id": "d92h7oq",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "16. WIND ENERGY – LIMITATIONS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "r393qbe",
      "content": "• Wind speed must be greater than 15 km/h."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5z1j2p8",
      "content": "• Large land area required."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fw0xo0g",
      "content": "• High initial installation cost."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "44yzm20",
      "content": "• Intermittent source (depends on wind availability)."
    },
    {
      "id": "xo12re2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "17. NUCLEAR FISSION & CHAIN REACTION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tjjfmqc",
      "content": "• In nuclear fission, heavy nucleus splits into smaller nuclei."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "s3547lk",
      "content": "• Enormous energy released (E = mc² concept)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yknrqaw",
      "content": "• Controlled chain reaction in reactor."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Wind mills require a minimum continuous wind speed of 15 km/h to sustain electricity generation.",
        "Heavy Water (D2O) and Graphite are used as moderators to slow down fast neutrons in a nuclear reactor.",
        "Hydrogen possesses the highest calorific value (~150,000 kJ/kg) among all known chemical fuels.",
        "Biogas mainly comprises methane (up to 75%), leaving behind a nutrient-rich slurry ideal for agricultural manure."
      ],
      "id": "usf623t"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ayp6ud5",
      "content": "• Uncontrolled chain reaction → Atomic bomb."
    },
    {
      "id": "zoe4abu",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "18. RADIOACTIVE WASTE MANAGEMENT"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qwf6s4v",
      "content": "• Nuclear waste remains radioactive for long period."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zqhv200",
      "content": "• Needs proper shielding and disposal."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0njvhbv",
      "content": "• Major drawback of nuclear power plants."
    },
    {
      "id": "3dkf2pn",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "19. ULTIMATE SOURCE OF ENERGY"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "k5nx1fl",
      "content": "• Sun is the ultimate source of almost all energy on Earth."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tvhmxcv",
      "content": "• Wind energy, hydro energy and fossil fuels indirectly depend on solar energy."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1tyivqd",
      "content": "• Tidal energy depends on gravitational pull of Moon."
    },
    {
      "id": "yf25058",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "20. ADVANCED RRB EXAM POINTS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "r77k6lm",
      "content": "• Nuclear fission releases enormous energy."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2kqdkxb",
      "content": "• Renewable sources are environment friendly."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7g9nbdj",
      "content": "• Biogas plant produces methane gas."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "n7dym2e",
      "content": "• Solar energy is ultimate source of most energy on Earth."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "e7staym",
      "content": "• Tidal energy depends on Moon’s gravitational pull."
    }
  ],
